  "lessons": [
    {
      "title": "Introduction",
      "slug": "introduction",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 52,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/circles.jpg\">",
              "legacyComponentId": 732,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div class=\"lead\">Welcome, {First}!</div>\r\n<b>Break out of the mold of rectangles and squares and try knitting in circles!</b><br><blockquote class=\"smallblock\">\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Machine knitted tree skirts are a great way to learn new techniques and improve your skills. (With a knitting machine, It’s never too early or late to think about Christmas knitting)<Br>\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-check\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Colorful knitted Circular pillows and throws make great gifts and will quickly spruce up your home.<br></blockquote>\r\n\r\nMake your circular knitting simple or as intricate as you like … you’re the designer! Incorporate color and stitch patterns for unique designs. The actual knitting isn’t hard, the fun comes in adding your own personal touches.<br>\r\n\r\nThis course includes 2 methods of creating circles. Use simple increases or decreases to create wedges. Or incorporate short row shaping and knit a skirt in one piece!<br>\r\n\r\nOnce you understand the techniques, you may even be inspired to knit a traditional hand knit style circular yoke sweater.<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\">\r\n\r\n<ul class=”Instruction-list”>\r\n<li>Pinwheel Circle (with shortrows)</li>\r\n<li>Increase Wedges</li>\r\n<li>Decrease Wedges</li>\r\n<li>Finishing Tips</li>\r\n<li>Inspiration</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nThis course will walk you through all the planning steps. It shows techniques that may be new to you and helps you record your progress.<br>If this is your first project or your tenth, follow along, the skills you gain here will be invaluable for future knitting projects .. not just circles!\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\">\r\nIf you are new here, the next lesson will help you learn to navigate this course so you can get the most benefit from the material that is included.\r\n</blockquote>",
              "legacyComponentId": 706,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Start Here",
          "slug": "start-here",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 232,
            "blockType": "Questions"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "The video will walk you through how to access the lessons and navigate to get the most out of your course.<br /> Don't skip lessons ... you may feel that you know how to cast on ... but sometimes you will pick up a tip that you can use while watching a video.<br><blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>Another reason to follow the course material in order - Throughout the lessons, you'll be making decisions about your blanket.  We will record your decisions to create your custom pattern and Course Binder.</em></blockquote>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 708,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "221120492",
              "title": "Machine Knitting Courses",
              "legacyComponentId": 709,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "How to use this course site",
          "slug": "how-to-use-this-course-site",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 233,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Blanket, Shawl, Tree Skirt, Pillow Cover -  your choice",
      "slug": "blanket-shawl-tree-skirt-pillow-cover-your-choice",
      "displayOrder": 30,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 53,
        "lessonOrder": 30
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Create a one-piece circular shape with short-rows. The bonus is a pinwheel design that is formed automatically! \r\n\r\n            \r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>Watch as we knit a pillow-top and discuss options for creating your own circles.</em></blockquote>\r\n\r\n                \r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/pinwheel_pillow_400.jpg\">   \r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/6wedge_shortrow.png\">   \r\n<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 713,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859578",
              "title": "Pinwheel Circles - Shortrow Fun",
              "legacyComponentId": 714,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Pinwheel Circles - Shortrow Fun",
          "slug": "pinwheel-circles-shortrow-fun",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 235,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Learn to create circular shapes with wedges. Knit each wedge in a different color, add motifs, cables or stitch patterns ...  the sky is the limit!<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>The tutorial includes using short-rows for curved edges. creating a more rounded shaped finished piece.</em></blockquote>\r\n\r\n                \r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/decrease_pillow.jpg\">   \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/wedges_thumb.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 715,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859583",
              "title": "Circles - Decreased Wedges",
              "legacyComponentId": 716,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Circles - Decrease Wedges",
          "slug": "circles-decrease-wedges",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 236,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Learn to create circular shapes with wedges. Knit each wedge in a different color, add motifs, cables or stitch patterns ...  the sky is the limit!<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>The tutorial includes using short-rows for curved edges. creating a more rounded shaped finished piece.</em></blockquote>\r\n\r\n                \r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/circle.png\">   \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/8wedge_INcrease.png\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 717,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859605",
              "title": "Circles - Increased Wedges",
              "legacyComponentId": 718,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Circles - Increased Wedges",
          "slug": "circles-increased-wedges",
          "order": 4,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 237,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Techniques",
      "slug": "techniques",
      "displayOrder": 40,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 55,
        "lessonOrder": 40
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Kitchener Stitch is the best way to join stitches to stitches. When knitting the short row pinwheel style circle, you will start and end with waste yarn.<br>\r\nNeatly join the 2 edges with Kitchener Stitch and no one will be know how you knit the circle in one piece on the machine!<br>\r\nYou may be familiar with Kitchener Stitch by hand, but have you tried working it on the machine?<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>Mastering this technique (on or off the machine) will be invaluable in your knitting learning journey</em></blockquote>\r\n<hr>\r\n<p class=\"lead\">Seaming from the purl side<br></p>",
              "legacyComponentId": 721,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151850342",
              "title": "Grafting on the Machine - Purl Side",
              "legacyComponentId": 722,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<hr>\r\n<p class=\"lead\">Seaming from the knit side</p>",
              "legacyComponentId": 723,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151849234",
              "title": "Grafting on the Machine - Knit Side",
              "legacyComponentId": 724,
              "order": 4
            }
          ],
          "title": "Kitchener Stitch Seaming",
          "slug": "kitchener-stitch-seaming",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 239,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Joining a panel of knitting to another panel as you knit, makes for fast finishing.  Using this technique will speed up the finishing of the blanket binding for this project.<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>If you've never tried sew-as-you-go, we recommend you take this opportunity to try it along the edge of a swatch.  This is a technique that you will use again and again in your knitting... not just for circles.</em>",
              "legacyComponentId": 725,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "169798401",
              "title": "Sew-as-you-go Tricks",
              "legacyComponentId": 726,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Sew-as-you-Go Tricks",
          "slug": "sew-as-you-go-tricks",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 240,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "A decorative sew-as-you-go method.\r\nJoin knitted panels neatly without sewing! This cable-look join is easy, adds dimension and style to your knitting. Great for machine knit afghans.<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 728,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859092",
              "title": "Twisted Join",
              "legacyComponentId": 729,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Twisted Join",
          "slug": "twisted-join",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 242,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858422",
              "title": "Seaming - Putting It All Together",
              "legacyComponentId": 727,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Seaming on the Machine",
          "slug": "seaming-on-the-machine",
          "order": 4,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 241,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "One Piece Pillow",
      "slug": "one-piece-pillow",
      "displayOrder": 50,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 54,
        "lessonOrder": 50
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<p class=\"lead\">\r\nCan you work short rows? You can finish this in a weekend!</p>\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>Quickly knit a 3 dimensional, pillow cover in one piece! Use variegated yarn, stripes or alternating colors to make it your own!</em></blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n                \r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles7.jpg\">   \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/pillow_drawing.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 735,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "imageGallery",
              "slides": [
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles1.jpg",
                  "caption": "Use a variegated yarn with long color repeats."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles2.jpg",
                  "caption": "Knit both sides of the pillow cover at the same time.  The \"points\" are the outside edge."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles3.jpg",
                  "caption": "Looking a bit strange ... but you are creating a large \"pocket\" to insert the pillow form."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles4.jpg",
                  "caption": "Off the machine ... only 1 opening to finish."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles5.jpg",
                  "caption": "Instead of scrapping off, the stitches were removed on a circular hand knitting needle.<br><small>(Lesson learned: Using a hand knitting needle to temporarily hold stitches is a nifty trick, in this case scrapping off would have been better for easier Kitchener stitch joining ... <em>live and learn ... </em>)</small>"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles6.jpg",
                  "caption": "Take time to neatly join the seam with the pillow form inserted"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/challenge/images/v2/10/circles/slideshow/circles7.jpg",
                  "caption": "Close the center hole on both sides and embellish with a button or flowers. The variegated yarn is really highlighted with the construction of this pillow."
                }
              ],
